Standard-conformance edits to the Hermes-Lite 2 radio core in
Hermes-Lite2-3e467fd-radioberry-pio.tar.xz (IEEE 1800-2005), applied by
tools/build.sh after unpacking it:

- radio.v: generate blocks RECEIVER2 and DEBUGRX, named like the parameters
  of the same names, renamed RECEIVER2_g and DEBUGRX_g.
- receiver.v, vna_scanner.v: body parameters CICRATE and RATE48 given a
  default (every instance sets them).
- radio.v: outputs assigned in always blocks declared output reg.
- radio.v, vna_scanner.v, receiver_nco.v: always @* blocks written
  always_comb, which also runs at time zero, so a simulator computes their
  outputs before the first clock as the hardware has them.

Both images are byte for byte the same with and without these edits.

